# SHA-256 digests of the Codex CLI release artefacts this fleet is allowed to run.
#
# Format: "<sha256>  <asset-name>", one per line — the same shape as
# scripts/copilot2api.sha256 and `sha256sum` output.
#
# A digest is established once, on a trusted host, after confirming the artefact's
# provenance against the upstream release, and then enforced everywhere:
#
#     bash scripts/fetch-codex.sh --record      # on a trusted host, once per pin
#     git add scripts/codex-cli.sha256 && commit
#
# `scripts/fetch-codex.sh` FAILS CLOSED for any asset without an entry here. That is
# deliberate: the point of the pin is that every runner executes the same bytes —
# runners sharing one ChatGPT account must not disagree about what `codex` is — and
# a placeholder digest committed ahead of time would only teach an operator to
# overwrite the expected value with whatever they had just downloaded.
#
# Version drift is caught independently of this file: `fetch-codex.sh` refuses to
# install a binary whose `--version` is not server/codex/schema.py's
# PINNED_CLI_VERSION, and the daemon re-generates and hashes the app-server JSON
# schema before offering Codex at all (server/codex/process.py:probe_availability).
#
# codex-cli 0.153.2 — recorded 2026-11-25 on dobby. Provenance: release rust-v0.153.2
# in openai/codex (org-owned, not a fork), asset uploaded by github-actions[bot];
# this digest equals GitHub's own asset digest and two independent downloads.
# openai/codex publishes no build attestations (`gh attestation verify` → 404).
# The npm package @openai/codex@0.153.2 vendors a byte-identical `codex` binary
# (sha256 f8786262…), verified on dobby, rocky and thready.
e8cd1160071f725d2a10cab81073dd6818fc8b096372125d27ef6e66fdf0979e  codex-x86_64-unknown-linux-musl.tar.gz
